.TH CTI-PATCHTUESDAY 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-patchtuesday \- build the monthly Microsoft Patch Tuesday synopsis and correlate it with the scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-patchtuesday
.RB [ \-\-month
.IR YYYY\-MM ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-text\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-manifest ]
.RB [ \-\-provider
.BR none ]
.RB [ \-\-url\-qualys
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-url\-bleeping
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-rows
.IR N ]
.PP
.B cti-patchtuesday
.RB [ \-\-month
.IR YYYY\-MM ]
.B \-\-subject\-only
.PP
.B cti-patchtuesday
.RB [ \-\-month
.IR YYYY\-MM ]
.BI \-\-explain " CVE"
.RI [ "source options" ]
.PP
.B cti-patchtuesday
.RB [ \-\-month
.IR YYYY\-MM ]
.B \-\-mark\-sent
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-patchtuesday
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-patchtuesday
writes the monthly synopsis of Microsoft's Patch Tuesday release. It is run by
.BR run\-patchtuesday (1)
from
.B cti\-agent\-patchtuesday.timer
at 07:30 on the Wednesday after the second Tuesday (the 9th to the 15th).
.PP
It reads two public wrap-ups: the Qualys security update review, at a URL
computed from the release date, and the BleepingComputer article, found by
trying the expected URL and then the site's Patch Tuesday tag listing. A
source that cannot be read is named on standard error and in the email; the
synopsis is still produced from the other. CVEs whose every sighting names a
product and none names a Microsoft one are scoped out of the release, and
listed on standard error. Where each headline figure came from is also
printed there.
.PP
It then maps the release's CVEs to Qualys QIDs through the KnowledgeBase
cache, adds the QIDs the Qualys review itself publishes, and asks Qualys Host
Detection, in batches of 300, which are open here. The email's table has one
row per detecting QID with the scanner's own host count. If the
KnowledgeBase cache cannot be loaded, the published QIDs alone are used. If
correlation fails altogether, or
.B \-\-provider none
is given, the synopsis still goes out with exposure marked
.BR "NOT MEASURED" ,
never as zero.
.PP
A month whose Patch Tuesday has not happened yet is refused, so an early run
cannot produce a confidently empty email.
.PP
.B cti-patchtuesday
does not send mail; the runner hands its output to the mailer.
.SS The release manifest
A normal run (no
.BR \-\-month ,
no
.BR \-\-dry\-run )
also writes
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/patchtuesday\-YYYY\-MM.json ,
0600, listing every CVE in the release and marked
.BR "sent: false" .
The daily digest holds back a release's CVEs only when this month's or last
month's manifest is marked sent, and only
.B \-\-mark\-sent
marks it.
.B run\-patchtuesday
calls
.B \-\-mark\-sent
after the mailer reports success and at no other time, so a synopsis that
never went out cannot silence the daily. A manifest that cannot be written is
a warning, not a failure: the daily simply keeps reporting those CVEs.
.PP
A
.B \-\-month
replay neither writes nor changes the manifest, because overwriting a sent
month would reset it to unsent.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-month ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-month " YYYY\-MM"
Report on this release instead of the most recent one, to replay a past
month and compare it with an email already sent. A replay does not touch the
manifest. Applies to
.B \-\-mark\-sent
and
.B \-\-subject\-only
too.
Default: this month if its Patch Tuesday has passed, otherwise last month.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the HTML email to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-out " FILE"
Write the plain-text version to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600. If neither
.B \-\-out
nor
.B \-\-text\-out
is given, the text version goes to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-json " FILE"
Write the structured digest to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600: the month, sources and parsed figures, exposure, the QQL used,
every detecting QID (the full list, not capped by
.BR \-\-max\-rows ),
and the subject including the exposure counts. It carries host names.
Not written with
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
Refused, exit 1, when
.I FILE
is the release manifest
.RI ( $FLEET_HOME/state/patchtuesday\-YYYY\-MM.json ),
which it would otherwise overwrite. Any other write failure is silently
ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the text version to standard output and stop: no
.BR \-\-out ,
no
.BR \-\-text\-out ,
no
.BR \-\-json ,
no manifest. The sources and Qualys are still queried.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-manifest
Write the report files but not the release manifest.
.B run\-patchtuesday \-\-dry\-run
passes this, because a manifest is a statement about what was sent and a
dry run that wrote one unsent over a sent one put the release's CVEs back
into the daily digest.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-subject\-only
Print the base subject line,
.BR "Microsoft Patch Tuesday for \fIMonth YYYY\fP" ,
and exit. Nothing is fetched, so the detection and host counts a full run
adds to the subject are never included.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-url\-qualys " URL"
Read the Qualys review from
.I URL
instead of the computed address, for when the blog's URL pattern changes.
Default:\~computed from the release date.
.TP
.BI \-\-url\-bleeping " URL"
Read the BleepingComputer article from
.I URL
instead of discovering it.
Default:\~discovered.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " NAME"
.B none
(any case) skips Qualys entirely: source parsing only, exposure
.BR "NOT MEASURED" .
Any other value, including empty, queries Qualys.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Timeout for each HTTP request to the sources, as a Go duration. The whole run
is bounded at five minutes regardless.
Default:\~\fB45s\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-rows " N"
Rows shown in the email's detection table, largest host count first.
.B 0
or less means 25. The full list is always in
.BR \-\-json .
Default:\~\fB0\fR (25).
.TP
.BI \-\-explain " CVE"
After reading the sources, print every place
.I CVE
was found on them and whether it was scoped out, then exit. Qualys is not
queried and nothing is written.
Default:\~none.
.TP
.B \-\-mark\-sent
Mark the month's manifest sent and exit, without fetching anything. Run only
after the synopsis has been delivered; the daily digest then holds back the
release's CVEs. Marking an already-sent manifest succeeds and changes
nothing. Refused, exit 2, together with
.BR \-\-dry\-run :
a dry run writes nothing, and this is a write.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the process environment, after
.I fleet.env
is loaded (existing environment variables win). Scanner settings are in
section 2 of
.IR fleet.env ,
paths in section 3, content in section 4. Graph credentials are not needed.
.TP
.BR QUALYS_BASE_URL ", " QUALYS_USERNAME ", " QUALYS_PASSWORD
Required for correlation when
.B LOOKUP_PROVIDER
is
.BR qualys .
Missing values do not stop the synopsis; exposure is reported as
.B NOT MEASURED
with the reason.
.TP
.B LOOKUP_PROVIDER
Default:\~\fBqualys\fR.
.TP
.B QUALYS_KB_CACHE
The CVE-to-QID KnowledgeBase cache.
Default:\~\fI./qualys_kb_cache.json\fR, relative to the working directory
.RI ( /var/lib/cti\-agent
under the units and the wrapper).
.TP
.B QUALYS_KB_MAX_AGE_HOURS
How old the cache may be before it is rebuilt. Default:\~\fB168\fR.
.TP
.BR GRAPH_LOOKBACK_HOURS ", " MAILBOX_LOOKBACK_HOURS ", " MAILBOX_MIN_AGE_HOURS
Not used here, but validated by the shared loader. An invalid value makes
correlation fail and exposure
.BR "NOT MEASURED" .
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
Where the manifest lives. Unset: no manifest is written (a note says so) and
.B \-\-mark\-sent
fails.
.TP
.B FLEET_ORG
Organisation name in the report. Default:\~\fBSecurity\fR.
.TP
.BR FLEET_ATTRIBUTION ", " FLEET_REPO_URL
The credit line at the foot of the email, linked to the URL. Only
.B http://
and
.B https://
URLs are used; anything else is reported and ignored. With only a URL, the
line reads
.IR "Correlated and published by the ORG Claude Code Agent Fleet" .
.TP
.B FLEET_ENV
The
.I fleet.env
path. Default:\~\fI$FLEET_HOME/fleet.env\fR, else
\fI/var/lib/cti\-agent/fleet.env\fR; the
.B cti\-agent
wrapper and the units set
.IR /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/patchtuesday\-YYYY\-MM.json
The release manifest, 0600. Delete it, or leave it unsent, and the daily
digest reports the release's CVEs as usual.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/patchtuesday\-*.html
.TQ
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/patchtuesday\-*.txt
The email written by
.BR run\-patchtuesday ,
0600.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/qualys_kb_cache.json
The KnowledgeBase cache, as set in the shipped
.IR fleet.env .
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
Settings and the Qualys credentials.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The synopsis was produced, even from one source, even with exposure not
measured, even if the manifest could not be written. Also: the subject or the
.B \-\-explain
report was printed, or the manifest was marked sent (or already was).
.TP
.B 1
Nothing usable was produced:
.B \-\-month
is not
.IR YYYY\-MM ;
that month's Patch Tuesday is in the future; neither source could be read;
or
.B \-\-out
or
.B \-\-text\-out
could not be written. For
.BR \-\-mark\-sent :
.B FLEET_HOME
is unset, there is no manifest for the month, or it cannot be read, parsed
or rewritten.
.TP
.B 2
.B \-\-mark\-sent
was given with
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
or an unknown option or bad value (Go's flag package).
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview this month's synopsis without writing anything:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-patchtuesday \-\-dry\-run | less
.EE
.PP
Through the runner: it renders the report files and writes the manifest
unsent, then calls the mailer with
.B \-\-dry\-run
and does not mark anything sent:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-patchtuesday \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
Replay August and compare it with the email that went out:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-patchtuesday \-\-month 2026\-08 \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
Why is a CVE counted (or not) in this release?
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-patchtuesday \-\-explain CVE\-2026\-12345
.EE
.PP
Source parsing only, when Qualys is down:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-patchtuesday \-\-provider none \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-patchtuesday (1),
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 11, "The monthly Patch Tuesday lane", and "The release
manifest".
